# Correlated memory delivery and complete joint readiness

**Primary-runner role: source integrity only.** The proposed primary checks exact proof bodies, mathematical-parent pins, selected recovery evidence and actual binding records. It does not run a physical model, prove a theorem, prepare a state or turn metadata into scientific evidence. It has not been executed in this source-only proposal. Scientific support is the analytic constructions, counterexamples and separately recorded source reviews preserved below.

The first result replaces exact product raw-memory and old-memory independence assumptions by a supplied full stationary binary Markov computational diagonal, allowing arbitrary coherences and correlations with every original factor and reference. A finite reversible NN word delivers approximately pure memory at the same fixed endpoints and supports the paid complete auxiliary/original-clock readiness protocol. The second result supplies a finite positive NN Hamiltonian with exactly that diagonal Gibbs law, explicit calibration allowances and a paid field removal on arbitrary correlated inputs. The second result does not produce its initial Gibbs state. These are separately accepted conditional results; their physical suppliers remain explicit.

This source-only regular-publication draft preserves seven complete historical proof/review bodies byte for byte. Current acceptance and mandatory interpretations are stated in this wrapper; historical pending statements inside attributed bodies remain unchanged. The two standalone root decisions are b62f977e and c2338e1a, sealed with verification 3343903a/freeze 4c85db1a. The separately checked composition is now accepted by decision 4d781ab6, verification 664293eb/freeze fbd981bc; its complete source and assessment are also preserved. Actual checkout/base binding, primary/cache/mutation/graph execution, publication and retained audit remain pending. No scientific program or historical science replay was performed for these new arguments or this package.

## Exact domain and what changes

Let D contain all original nonclock factors, X the original M-site clock, A the complete three-component mediator, S=A union X, and R all passive references. Let s=|S|. Keep the first s sites E of the existing joint-readiness +x ray fixed, extend that ray to B=EF, and retain every spacer and garbage factor F. For Z=D S R, the initial rho_ZB is arbitrary except for its entire computational-basis B diagonal:

    p(x)=pi_(x1) product_i P_(xi,x(i+1)),
    P=[[1-a,a],[b,1-b]], q=a/(a+b)<1/2,
    pi=(1-q,q), lambda=1-a-b, |lambda|<1.

The Markov result permits its stated boundary cases, including q=0, and requires quantitative certificates for finite effective selection. The Gibbs construction has the narrower interior domain 0<a<b<1 and beta>0. Neither theorem assumes the diagonal promise conditionally on a reference outcome. No original factor is moved, no old data/apparatus record is initialized for free, and no N_X=1 hypothesis is imposed on the arbitrary initial S register. A specified normalized computable one-excitation packet is synthesized later by the paid parent controls.

The retired premises are exact product structure of the raw bits and independence from the old system. The full correlated diagonal, its basis, bias/mixing margins, fresh factors, controls, isolation and calibration remain supplied. A one-site bias estimate, an abstract realized-state slot, or a temperature label does not certify that full diagonal. The registered realized-state primitive is an approved reference interface; it does not supply this state-dependent distribution or its values. No axiom or primitive is added.

## Fixed-endpoint domination and reversible compression

For q<q_bar<1/2 and |lambda|<=lambda_bar<1, choose ell>=1 with lambda_bar^ell<=q_bar-q. Directly,

    P^d(x,1)=q+lambda^d(x-q)<=q_bar,  d>=ell.

Every ordered selected set with gaps at least ell is therefore dominated by iid Bernoulli(q_bar) variables through a common independent-uniform threshold coupling. This holds for negative lambda and does not require monotonicity of the transition kernel in its previous bit. Recursive ternary majority is increasing, so its failure probability is bounded by

    q_0=q_bar, q_(k+1)=3q_k^2-2q_k^3.

Choose r>=1, Q=3^r, and leaves

    x_(j,0)=j,
    x_(j,t)=s+[(j-1)(Q-1)+t]ell, 1<=t<Q,
    L_raw=s+s(Q-1)ell.

The first gap is ell+h_j, h_j=s-j+(j-1)(Q-1)ell>=0; later gaps are ell. These disjoint sets retain E_j as their first representatives. A union bound gives p_bad<=min(1,s q_r). The outputs need not be independent. A different pre-exposure derivation uses interleaved uniform strides and a TV telescoping allowance; its distinct sufficient resource formula is preserved rather than silently identified with this layout.

Chronological CX(a,b), CX(a,c), CCX(b,c;a) gives majority at a and reversible garbage elsewhere. The full positive two-qubit CV/CX word for CCX is phase exact. Returned SWAP routing at distance d uses 2d-1 two-qubit gates and acts as identity on all intermediate dirty, entangled factors after each completed gate. No clean routing work bit or discarded output is used. Compression extends the earlier pure-memory readiness dictionary by supplied CX/CV controls, including ZX and onsite channels; static hopping alone does not supply them.

For this nonuniform leaf layout the exact counts are

    P_c=(20ell r/3)sQ-(7/2)s(Q-1)
                     +5r s(s-1)[1+(Q-1)ell],
    D_c=ell[(s-1)(Q-1)+2Q/3],
    A_c=pi[P_c+s(Q-1)/4].

There are s(Q-1)/2 logical majority nodes. Each has seven pair distances summing to 10ell 3^(k-1), with the additional five incidences of its displaced first representative charged in P_c. The positive logarithm norms are pi for full SWAP and CX, 3pi/2 for CV, and pi/2 for CV-dagger. Their physical identity coefficients total exactly A_c/4. Dropping these offsets changes the phase-exact word and scalar ledger. Full SWAP includes ZZ and applies to arbitrary old states.

Finite stopping follows from the majority recurrence below 1/2 and the supplied quantitative margins. The costs are not uniform as q approaches 1/2, |lambda| approaches 1, precision increases or s grows. Finite existence is not a common-cap feasibility certificate or a native method of estimating the input parameters.

## Exact actual marginal versus the ideal readiness target

For any actual compressed sigma_EY, Y=ZF, let p=1-Tr[(|0_E><0_E| tensor I_Y)sigma] and omega_actual=Tr_E sigma. Then

    ||sigma-|0_E><0_E| tensor omega_actual||_1
       <=g(p)=p+sqrt(p(4-3p))<=3sqrt(p).

This retains exactly the whole unconditioned Y marginal. It does not normalize a successful block, discard F, guarantee purity after conditioning on a rare reference outcome, or implement an erase channel. A purification of the allowed diagonal attains g(p), so replacing it by 2sqrt(p) is not valid for this exact-marginal target. Event TV is half classical L1; all quantum trace distances here are unhalved.

If a physical compression output is within full trace distance d_c of the ideal output, its event probability is at most min(1,p_bound+d_c/2). The same lemma applies with that actual event and actual marginal. Alternatively, changing the ideal-marginal comparator to the actual one by triangle inequality costs at most g(p_bound)+2d_c, capped at 2. It is not g(p_bound)+d_c. A theorem keeping a fixed ideal target does not acquire an extra doubled error merely from this alternative comparison.

For the complete compensated protocol, let omega_ideal be the marginal of the ideal memory-only compression of the stated input. The full H0-aged target uses omega_ideal: all former S records move to E, A becomes vacuum, X becomes the supplied packet, D ages under H0 for the actual complete duration T, and F/R remain. A finite actual turn-on can alter ZF through F_inst, so its midpoint marginal is generally different from H0-aged omega_ideal. The full-space turn-on allowance pays that difference. The exact-actual-marginal lemma and this ideal H0-aged endpoint contract are distinct statements.

Write the installed generator K=H0+F_inst and positive compensators C=sum_alpha(c_alpha I-h_alpha)=kappa I-F_inst, c_alpha>=||h_alpha||. The nominal controls give

    H(t)=H0+(1-u)F_inst+u kappa I+G(t).

The unchanged H0 is never canceled. During turn-on, B_F>=||F_inst|| is a full-space bound. The plateau implements compression, then the pure-E comparison, then returned reset and clock synthesis. Only after that comparison may the ready-range bound Gamma>=||F_inst J_ready|| be used during release. The complete trace price is

    min(2,eta+e_mem+B_F r_on+Gamma r_off
                       +2 integral_0^T ||E_impl(t)||dt).

Every compression, routing, synthesis and ramp duration contributes to T and actual H0 aging. The input allowance eta is used for this fixed target; no success-sector assumption is imposed on the actual faulty trajectory. E contains displaced records afterward and is not certified fresh for reuse.

## Full release operator, scalar and physical prices

The readiness calculation retains K_X psi and the clock/source covariance. With the frozen source's

    T_X=K_X+sum_j S_j n_j,
    B_D=(S0+R0)I-sum_i d_i Pe_i,
    mu=<T_X>, chi=sum_i q_i^2+sum_(i,j)|z_ij|^2|psi_j|^2,
    nu=Var(T_X)+Delta chi, A0=B_D+mu I,

one has J_ready*F_inst J_ready=A0 and J_ready*F_inst^2 J_ready=A0^2+nu I, so Gamma=sqrt(||A0||^2+nu). Both data-source and clock-source squares remain. The K_X/counterterm covariance is inside Var(T_X); the H0/B_D covariance remains in endpoint moments. If the installed baseline is enlarged to act on E/F, this scalar simplification must be rederived or replaced by the safe Gamma=B_F.

The literal compensation dictionary has 2m+8M+14 blocks. Its Pauli scalar includes M/(2a_c), every auxiliary diagonal load, S0, half the clock-counterterm sum and R0. Pe is a traceless Pauli, so Pe n_b and -d Pe add no full scalar. The complete added scalar action is

    (kappa-s_Finst)A_u+A_c/4+P_J pi/4+pi/2+Theta+ell_phi/2,

where A_u includes the whole compression plateau. The ideal endpoint map phase is exp[-i(kappa A_u+Theta)]; a ledger of physical identity coefficients is not a replacement for that phase-exact operator identity.

For the actual flat unit-area pulse w and a positive gate logarithm Lambda_g, whole-block peak, slew and variation are m0||Lambda_g||/tau_g, m1||Lambda_g||/tau_g^2 and 2m0||Lambda_g||/tau_g. Compensation peak/action/variation are at most B_C, B_C A_u and 2B_C when B_C is an upper bound. Joint routing uses P_J=s^2+2sum_j ell_j<=3s^2-2s; the total gate count is P_c+P_J+M+1 and action is A_c+pi(P_J+1)+2Theta+ell_phi.

A separately calibrated rotation has channel sum at most (1+sqrt(5))theta, rather than its whole-block norm 2theta. The corresponding equal-slot channel peak uses (1+sqrt(5))pi, not the 3pi block maximum. Literal compensation channel sum can be bounded by (5/2)kappa. All onsite, quadrature and scalar errors are summed. For simultaneous coefficient/envelope errors, the product term remains; timing translations require actual endpoint guards or repriced elapsed time. Persistent residuals are part of the actual baseline, not vanished pulses.

The fixed ray root is (X_*+q_c,Y_*+q_c,4), and B_j=root+(j,0,0). X_* remains determined by the old inventory. The first new site has the already identified extra adjacency to the outer z=3 cycle; later sites lie beyond the base maxima. Only consecutive ray adjacencies are newly present thereafter. The complete isolation set subtracts all declared edges from every geometric NN pair touching S or B; the declared count is m+4M+L_raw+9 and the safe omission count is at most 6(s+L_raw). Same-component chords, intercomponent and fresh-old edges, new fields and all physical scalings remain charged. Freshness is not isolation. Extra occupied factors require an enlarged actual inventory.

For trace error epsilon and beta>=||K-alpha I||, centered scalar first/second moments and variance have bounds beta epsilon, beta^2 epsilon and 3beta^2 epsilon. Retained ordered moments are explicitly centered partial traces; general norm-duality tests are required if they are non-Hermitian. Raw moments restore alpha Delta rho_Y and 2alpha Delta M_1^c+alpha^2 Delta rho_Y. The scalar-K routing-fault witness prevents deleting these marginal terms. These linear records are not a conditional variance or a physical energy measurement.

Work bounds require differentiable controls and the actual endpoint baseline, plus variation/derivative information. Small integrated error alone does not bound work or slew. Commutation of a memory drive with an old generator factors evolution but does not eliminate covariance on correlated inputs. Full unitary entropy and records remain; the Markov Shannon entropy need not equal quantum entropy for coherent inputs. No consumption/recycling or controller-energy supply is derived.

## Separately accepted finite Gibbs delivery interface

For the interior Markov domain, define Q_xy=sqrt(pi_x)P_xy/sqrt(pi_y), with Q_00=1-a, Q_11=1-b and Q_01=Q_10=sqrt(ab). Q is **entrywise positive**; its eigenvalue lambda can be negative, so operator positivity is not assumed. With adjacent diagonal energies e_xy=-log Q_xy/beta and endpoint energies e_x=-log pi_x/(2beta),

    H_B=sum_i h_(i,i+1)+g_1+g_L,
    exp(-beta H_B)=diag(p), Tr exp(-beta H_B)=1.

The endpoint factors and scalar offsets are indispensable to this literal identity. Every local h and g is positive on its full qubit domain. Each edge is dI+u(Z_i+Z_(i+1))+v Z_i Z_(i+1), with d=(e00+2e01+e11)/4, u=(e00-e11)/4 and v=(e00-2e01+e11)/4. Endpoint g=cI+wZ gives the complete scalar (L-1)d+2c, endpoint fields u+w and interior fields 2u. Componentwise logarithms, not a matrix logarithm, are used.

For mu=min(1-a,1-b,sqrt(ab)), ||H_B||<=[(L-1)(-log mu)-log q]/beta. The complete literal channel allowance is (L-1)(|d|+2|u|+|v|)+2(|c|+|w|). At fixed nonsingular parameters these are O(L), with no uniform singular-limit or cap claim.

For strictly positive laws, event TV is bounded by tanh(R/4), R=osc log(p'/p). For an actual diagonal Gibbs generator G_B=H_B+V_B+kI at beta'>0,

    R<=beta' osc(V_B)+|beta'-beta|osc(H_B)
      <=2beta' sum_j epsilon_j+|beta'-beta|kappa_B.

A delivered diagonal allowance d_prep gives d_diag<=min(1,d_prep+tanh(R/4)). This uses the complete ray and local-error sum. Noncommuting perturbations need a different stability result. A scalar reserve k affects neither the normalized diagonal nor R but remains in norms, phase and work. Engineering H_B anew while changing beta is different from temperature error in one fixed apparatus.

For separated old K_Z and memory G_B, a supplied nonincreasing switch with 0<=u<=1 and exact endpoints u(0)=1, u(t_q)=0 gives exactly

    U_q=e^(-it_q K_Z) tensor e^(-i A_q G_B), A_q=integral u.

It preserves the full memory diagonal and retains all correlation phases on arbitrary rho_ZB. A commuting Gibbs memory marginal is unchanged, not newly purified. Its field prices are action A_q||G_B||, peak ||G_B||, slew ||u'||_infinity||G_B|| and variation ||G_B||. The formal work is -Tr(G_B rho_B), including the scalar reserve. For diag(p), beta<H_B>=h(q)+(L-1)[(1-q)h(a)+qh(b)]; coherent states with the same diagonal need not have that entropy. This bookkeeping does not identify a physical work store, yield, Landauer cost or thermalization mechanism.

A supplied phase-exact permutation consumer converts d_diag to bad probability at most delta_0+d_diag and uses the exact remaining marginal with g(delta). Its positive physical duration must bring its actual-generator, routing, phase, fault and aging contract. Abstract C_B cannot erase that duration. Subsequent H0 evolution follows the actual K_Z aging chronologically. Independently supplied calibrated onsite and NN diagonal coefficients, their signs and scalars are required: a full-SWAP gate alone does not supply independently adjustable static ZZ fields. Smooth endpoints alone do not establish the stated switch peak or variation.

The finite probability machinery is established context. The source credits [Mei Yin](https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.1789) for Markov/Gibbs context and [Cohen–Fausti](https://arxiv.org/html/2309.02413v2) for the sharp likelihood-ratio bound, using equation (39) with the unhalved-to-event-TV conversion. Exact finite proofs are supplied here. Targeted primary passages, not entire papers or a comprehensive novelty survey, were read; remote papers are not purportedly byte archived. No infinite-volume boundary convention is imported.

## Checked Gibbs-to-Markov composition and its actual target

The separate composition source 6296fd36 and complete assessment 406f011c join the supplied interfaces on the same raw length L_raw; this follows from their own source decision, not the earlier standalone acceptances alone. The Gibbs interior domain satisfies the Markov domain, and the selected L_raw>=3 satisfies the finite Gibbs endpoint construction. The approximate delivered diagonal need not itself be Markov or stationary. Only its global event-TV distance from the designed p is used: the inverse bad-event projector of the completed exact permutation is diagonal, so

    delta_bar=min(1,s q_r+d_diag).

Let rho_q=(e^(-it_q K_Z) tensor e^(-iA_q G_B))rho(...)* be the nominal post-quench full state, rho_c=U_c rho_q U_c*, and omega=Tr_E rho_c. This retains the diagonal phases before compression; they cannot be deleted from the quantum target merely because the diagonal law is unchanged. The pure-E comparison preserves exactly this nominal post-quench ideal compression marginal and costs g(delta_bar).

The compensated physical consumer has actual duration T_p, including compression, routing, synthesis and both ramps. After relabeling S into E, the original-record marginal of its ideal target is

    e^(-i T_p H0)e^(-i t_q K_Z) rho_Z
                   e^(i t_q K_Z)e^(i T_p H0).

No commutation of K_Z and H0 is assumed. Every extra wait or physical segment enters this ordered target with its actual generator and duration. A wait after field removal and before compensation contributes K_Z aging, not free H0 aging. The actual faulty midpoint marginal is a different comparator, handled by its own event probability or the safe two-sided triangle allowance above.

For complete actual-minus-nominal residuals E_q and E_p on the entire enlarged system, the checked composed trace bound is

    min(2,g(delta_bar)+B_F r_on+Gamma r_off
                    +2 integral||E_q(t)||dt
                    +2 integral||E_p(t)||dt).

The full-space turn-on bound precedes the pure-E substitution; the ready-range release bound follows it. The diagonal allowance is not charged again as a full-state Gibbs approximation. Modeled V_B already belongs to G_B; additional dynamic errors must name their reference generator to avoid double counting. Any surviving endpoint memory field enters the next actual generator or its full-duration residual.

A fixed nonzero d_diag leaves a floor in this sufficient estimate; increasing the compressor alone does not remove it. For 0<epsilon<1, sufficient allocations s q_r<=epsilon^2/72 and d_diag<=epsilon^2/72 make g(delta_bar)<=epsilon/2. Allocate the remaining dynamic/ramp terms at most epsilon/2. One compatible thermal allocation is d_prep<=epsilon^2/144 and 2beta' sum_j epsilon_j+|beta'-beta|kappa_B<=4artanh(epsilon^2/144). These are sufficient bounds, not optimality or an unavoidable physical lower bound. The raw length fixes kappa_B, so temperature and total local calibration must be budgeted after that length is selected.

The actual nominal protocol begins with K_Z+G_B and ends with K_Z. It therefore has different initial and final memory Hamiltonians. Its formal work is W_q+W_p, where W_q=-Tr(G_B rho_B) and W_p is the readiness stage's actual same-baseline endpoint energy difference. The quench scalar a_G A_q and full readiness scalar action both remain; nominal positivity requires the stated positive baselines, decompositions and envelopes. This is not a closed same-baseline cycle, gauge-independent harvested work, thermalization process or restored raw-memory resource. Fault-dependent work needs actual endpoint and derivative information beyond a state-error integral.

